<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diarmait Mac Murchada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1110–<a href="/years/1171">1171</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Dermot MacMurrough</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diarmait Mac Murchada was King of Leinster of the Uí Chennselaig dynasty. Driven out by the High King Ruaidrí Ua Conchobair and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigernan-ua-ruairc">Tigernán Ua Ruairc</a> in 1166, he sought help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> and recruited Anglo-Norman knights, above all Richard de Clare, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a>, who married his daughter Aoife. Their capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> in 1170 began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-norman-invasion-of-ireland">Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada.jpg" alt="Diarmait Mac Murchada" width="262" height="720" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giraldus Cambrensis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diarmaid_Mac_Murrough_Expugnatio_Hibernica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
